                        


Item #:  SCP-5974

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5974 is to be kept in a bullet proof glass case in an empty room, which should be monitored at all times. SCP-5974 is to be emptied of all contents and refilled with warm, freshly made black coffee every 24 hours.

Description:  SCP-5974 is a 24 ounce █████████ coffee cup that has no visible wear on it. Although the size remains constant, the design tends to change according to the current design of the seasonal cup.

When the coffee is left unchanged for more than 24 hours, SCP-5974 causes the nearest entity3 Once the embedding process has finished, SCP-5974-2 will become enraged and gain large amounts of strength, killing everything it sees until it expires, either by external forces, or exhaustion. Once SCP-5974-2 has expired, it will explode leaving only splatters of blood, and an unscathed SCP-5974 on the floor.

SCP-5974 was found on March 20, 1997 in San Diego California. The search for SCP-5974 started after reports of people mysteriously going missing in multiple places between San Diego California, and Phoenix Arizona.4

